{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01QG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Gamma_*(X, \\mathcal{L})$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\Gamma_*(X, \\mathcal{L}, \\mathcal{F}) =\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\in \\mathbf{Z}}\n\\Gamma(X, \\mathcal{F} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_X} \\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes n}).\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0009": "$X = \\mathbf{P}^n_R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-definition-gamma-star}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{situation-ample}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{constructions-lemma-quasi-coherent-projective-space}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0f186203c717db3a586b074367b5557c1e97d3ae984cd6b2c37f21857f1780ba", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a696bc8fc1698b757aa1cf62c80de716a3ea2b76a63e1938520b1aa72da9f311", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall from Modules, Definition <REF_0001>\nthat given a locally ringed space <MATH_0001>, an invertible sheaf <MATH_0002>,\nand a <MATH_0003>-module <MATH_0004> we have the graded\n<MATH_0005>-module\n<MATH_0006>\nThe following lemma says that, in Situation <REF_0002>,\nwe can recover a quasi-coherent <MATH_0007>-module <MATH_0008>\nfrom this graded module. Take a look also at\nConstructions, Lemma <REF_0003>\nwhere we prove this lemma in the special case <MATH_0009>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f9a979c8760a3a189430bf9a9cd43391f13d4d2dba4d5178a2cf6e7619651232", "unit_id": "tag:01QG:prose-0003"}
